hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21484","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us. Abdullah narrated to us, saying: And my father narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl: Suwayd ibn Ghafalah narrated to me, saying: I went out with Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabiah, until when we were at al-Udhayb I picked up a whip, so they said to me: Throw it away, but I refused. When I came to Madinah I met Ubayy ibn Kab and mentioned that to him, so he said: I picked up a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he said: Announce it a year. So I announced it a year and found none who knew it. He said: So he said: Know its number and its container and its tie, then announce it a year, and if its owner comes, else it is as the way of your wealth. And this is the wording of Waki. And Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: So he said: Announce it. So I announced it a year, then came to him, so he said: Announce it. So I announced it a year, then came to him, so he said: Announce it. So I announced it a year, then came to him, so he said: Know its count and its container and its tie, and if one comes informing you of its count and its container and its tie, give it to him, else enjoy it."
"21485","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl who said: I heard Suwayd ibn Ghafalah. And Abdullah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me: Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Shubah: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, saying: I heard Suwayd ibn Ghafalah who said: I raided with Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabiah, and found a whip and took it, so they said to me: Cast it away. I said: No, but I shall announce it, and if I find who knows it, else I shall enjoy it. They insisted upon me and I insisted upon them. When we returned from our raid I performed Hajj and came to Madinah and met Ubayy ibn Kab and mentioned to him their saying and my saying to them, so he said: I found a purse in it a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: Announce it a year. So I announced it a year and found none who knew it. So I came to him and said to him: I found none who knew it. So he said: Announce it a year, three times, and I know not whether he said that to him in a year or in three years. So he said to me in the fourth: Know its number and its tie, and if you find who knows it, else enjoy it. And this is the wording of Yahya ibn Saeed's hadith. And Muhammad ibn Jafar added in his hadith, saying: So I met him after that in Makkah, and he said: I know not, three years or one year."
"21486","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us from al-Amash from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah who said: We were pilgrims, and I found a whip and took it, so the people said: You take it, perhaps it belongs to a Muslim man. He said: So I said: Is it not for me to take it and benefit by it, better than the wolf devour it. So I met Ubayy ibn Kab and mentioned that to him, so he said: You did well. Then he said: I picked up a purse in it a hundred dinars, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: Announce it a year. So I announced it a year, then came to him and said: I announced it a year. So he said: Announce it another year. Then he said: Benefit by it, and keep its tie and its cloth and count its number, and if its owner comes. Jarir said: I did not retain what is after this, meaning the completion of the hadith."
"21487","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us from al-Amash from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah who said: We were pilgrims, and I found a whip and took it, so the people said: You take it, perhaps it belongs to a Muslim man. He said: So I said: Is it not for me to take it and benefit by it, better than the wolf devour it. So I met Ubayy ibn Kab and mentioned that to him, so he said: You did well. Then he said: I picked up a purse in it a hundred dinars, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: Announce it a year. So I announced it a year, then came to him and said: I announced it a year. So he said: Announce it another year. Then he said: Benefit by it, and keep its tie and its cloth and count its number, and if its owner comes. Jarir said: I did not retain what is after this, meaning the completion of the hadith."
"21488","Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Rashid al-Basri narrated to me: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I picked up a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Announce it a year. So I announced it a year, then came to him and said: I announced it a year. He said: Announce it another year. So I announced it another year, then came to him in the third, so he said: Count its number and its tie and enjoy it."
"21489","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us. And Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah who said: I performed Hajj, I and Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabiah, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: So I announced it two years or three. He said: Know its number and its container and its tie and enjoy it, and if its owner comes and knows its count and its tie, give it to him."
